## 2.2 SAP Work Processes — Complete Reference

### Work Process Types Table:
```
╔═══════╦══════════════╦══════╦═══════════════════════════════════════╗
║ Code  ║ Name         ║ Min  ║ Description                           ║
╠═══════╬══════════════╬══════╬═══════════════════════════════════════╣
║ DIA   ║ Dialog       ║  2   ║ Handles interactive user requests     ║
║ BTC   ║ Background   ║  1   ║ Executes scheduled batch jobs         ║
║ UPD   ║ Update (V1)  ║  1   ║ Asynchronous DB updates (primary)    ║
║ UP2   ║ Update (V2)  ║  0   ║ Secondary/statistical DB updates      ║
║ ENQ   ║ Enqueue      ║  1   ║ Manages SAP logical lock table        ║
║ SPO   ║ Spool        ║  1   ║ Manages print output and spool        ║
║ MSG   ║ Message      ║  1   ║ Load balancing, logon groups          ║
║ GW    ║ Gateway      ║  1   ║ RFC/CPIC connections                  ║
║ ICM   ║ ICM          ║  1   ║ HTTP/HTTPS for web applications       ║
╚═══════╩══════════════╩══════╩═══════════════════════════════════════╝
```

### Work Process Profile Parameters:
```
rdisp/wp_no_dia  = 10  ← Number of Dialog work processes
rdisp/wp_no_btc  = 5   ← Number of Background work processes
rdisp/wp_no_upd  = 2   ← Number of Update work processes
rdisp/wp_no_up2  = 1   ← Number of Update-2 work processes
rdisp/wp_no_enq  = 1   ← Number of Enqueue work processes
rdisp/wp_no_spo  = 2   ← Number of Spool work processes
```

### Work Process States (SM50/SM66):
```
State     Symbol  Meaning
────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Wait      ✅      Idle — ready to process new request
Run       ✅      Currently executing a user/job request
Hold      ⚠️      Waiting for DB response / RFC / lock
Stop      ❌      Stopped — investigate trace file
PRIV      ❌      Exclusive private memory — check program!
Ended     ❌      Process died — SAP will auto-restart
```

> 💡 **PRIV State Example:**
> - User runs a report that loads millions of records
> - Report exceeds Extended Memory → moves to Heap (PRIV)
> - WP is now exclusively tied to that user
> - **Fix:** Optimize program to use less memory, or increase `em/initial_size_MB`

