## 2.3 SAP System Identification

### System ID (SID):
```
Rules:
  ► Exactly 3 characters (letters and numbers)
  ► Must start with a letter
  ► Cannot use reserved names

Reserved SIDs (NEVER use):
  ADD, ALL, AND, ANY, ASC, COM, DBA, END, EPS, FOR,
  GID, IBM, INT, KEY, LOG, MON, NIX, NOT, NUL, OFF,
  OMS, RAW, ROW, SAP, SET, SGA, SHG, SID, SQL, SYS,
  TMP, UID, UNI, USR, VAR

Valid Examples:
  DEV (Development)  QAS (Quality)  PRD (Production)
  D01, T01, P01     S4D (S/4HANA Dev)
```

### Instance Number:
```
2-digit number (00–99) identifying an instance on a host

Port Number Formula:
  Dispatcher Port    : 32<NN>   → 00 = 3200, 01 = 3201
  Message Server     : 36<NN>   → 00 = 3600, 01 = 3601
  SAP Gateway        : 33<NN>   → 00 = 3300, 01 = 3301
  ICM HTTP           : 80<NN>   → 00 = 8000, 01 = 8001
  ICM HTTPS          : 443<NN>  → 00 = 44300
```

