## 5.1 SAP Logon Groups (SMLG)

Logon Groups allow load balancing of users across multiple application servers.

```
Transaction: SMLG → Maintain Logon Groups

WITHOUT Logon Groups:                WITH Logon Groups:
─────────────────────                ────────────────────
All users → App Server 1             Group "DIALOG":
(Server 1 overloaded!)                 → App Server 1 (50 users max)
                                       → App Server 2 (50 users max)
                                     Group "BATCH":
                                       → App Server 3 (batch jobs only)

Creating a Logon Group:
  SMLG → Create
  Group Name   : DIALOG
  Instance     : DEV_DVEBMGS00_server1
  Limits:
    Max Users  : 50    (0 = unlimited)
    Max Resp.  : 3000  (milliseconds - max response time)
```

## 5.2 Operation Modes (RZ04/SM63)

Operation Modes define how work processes are distributed **at different times of day**.

```
Transaction: RZ04 → Define Operation Modes
Transaction: SM63 → Set Operation Mode Timetable

CONCEPT:
  DAY MODE (08:00-18:00):
    DIA = 12  BTC = 3  (More dialog for users)
    
  NIGHT MODE (18:00-08:00):
    DIA = 3   BTC = 12  (More background for batch jobs)

Creating an Operation Mode:
Step 1: RZ04 → Create two modes: DAY_MODE, NIGHT_MODE
Step 2: Define WP distribution for each mode
Step 3: SM63 → Set timetable:
         Monday-Friday 08:00 → Switch to DAY_MODE
         Monday-Friday 18:00 → Switch to NIGHT_MODE
         Saturday 00:00 → NIGHT_MODE (all batch)

Benefits:
  ✅ Maximize dialog performance during business hours
  ✅ Maximize batch throughput overnight
  ✅ Fully automatic — no manual intervention
```

## 5.3 SAP License Administration (SLICENSE)

```
Transaction: SLICENSE → License Administration

SAP License Key:
  ► Every SAP system requires a valid license
  ► Tied to: Hardware key (from the installation server)
  ► Type: DEVELOPER, PROFESSIONAL, NAMED USER, etc.

Checking License:
  SLICENSE → Shows:
    - License validity date
    - Number of licensed users
    - Current system hardware key
    - License type

Installing New License:
  1. Get Hardware Key from SLICENSE
  2. Go to SAP Support Portal → License Keys
  3. Generate new license key file (.TXT)
  4. SLICENSE → Install → Upload the .TXT file
  5. Verify new expiry date

⚠️ License expiry = System lockout!
   Monitor: Schedule alert 4 weeks before expiry
```

## 5.4 SAP System Parameters Overview (RZ11)

```
Transaction: RZ11 → Profile Parameter Documentation

Essential for SAP Basis:
  ► Look up any parameter's: purpose, valid values, default
  ► See if parameter requires restart
  ► Check current vs. configured value

Dynamic Parameters (No Restart Needed):
  ► Can be changed with: Transaction RZ10 or
  ► OS: kill -USR1 <dispatcher_pid>  (Unix)

Static Parameters (Restart Required):
  ► Must restart the SAP instance
  ► Plan a maintenance window for these!

Key Parameter Groups:
