## 7.4 Update Monitor (SM13)

```
Transaction: SM13 → Update Records Overview

What is an Update?
  When a user saves data in SAP, the actual DB write
  can be done ASYNCHRONOUSLY by the Update Work Process.
  
  User Action → Dialog WP → Queues Update → UPD WP → Database

Update Status Values:
  Run  → Currently being processed
  Init → Initialized, waiting for UPD work process
  Auto → Automatic retry
  Err  → ❌ ERROR! Update failed! Action required!

Handling Update Errors (SM13 → Status = Err):
  Step 1: Double-click to see error details
  Step 2: Analyze: Is it a data issue or DB issue?
  Step 3: Options:
    ► Repeat → Retry the update (if transient error)
    ► Delete → Delete the update (if cannot be fixed)
    ► Investigate with SE38/SM21 for root cause
    
⚠️ Update errors mean data was NOT saved to database!
   Business team MUST be informed of update errors!
```

## 7.5 Lock Entries (SM12)

```
Transaction: SM12 → Lock Entry List

SAP Lock Types:
  E = Exclusive     → Only ONE user can access
  S = Shared        → Multiple users can read simultaneously
  X = Exclusive non-cumulative → Special exclusive lock
  O = Optimistic    → Set until first write operation

Normal Lock Scenario:
  User opens FB01 (Post FI Document)
  → Lock created on document key
  → User saves → Lock released automatically
  → OK ✅

Stale Lock Scenario (Problem!):
  User crashes mid-transaction
  → Lock remains even though session is gone
  → Other users blocked!
  → Action: Delete the stale lock (SM12 → select → delete)

⚠️ Before deleting locks ALWAYS verify:
   1. The lock owner is no longer active (check SM04/AL08)
   2. Consult business owner if unsure
   3. Document what you deleted and why
```

