## 9.1 SAP Spool Architecture

```
HOW SPOOL WORKS IN SAP:
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
User executes a report with print option
              ↓
SAP creates a SPOOL REQUEST (stored in TemSe)
              ↓
Output Request created (sent to output queue)
              ↓
Spool Work Process (SPO) processes the request
              ↓
Sends formatted output to Output Device (printer)
              ↓
Physical printing at printer

TemSe = Temporary Sequential Object Storage
        ► Stores spool data in DB table TST01/TST03
        ► Managed via transaction SP12
        ► Default retention: 8 days
```

