## 10.1 Background Processing Architecture

```
WHY BACKGROUND JOBS?
────────────────────────────────────────────────────
► Long-running programs (hours) → can't tie up dialog WPs
► Scheduled automation → no human needed
► Off-peak execution → nights, weekends
► High data volumes → month-end closing, payroll runs
► No user interaction required
► Can run on specific application servers

BACKGROUND JOB FLOW:
User/Admin schedules job (SM36)
         ↓
Job stored in TBTCO/TBTCP tables
         ↓
SAP event checker (every 60 seconds)
         ↓
Job trigger time reached → Status: Ready
         ↓
Background WP picks up job
         ↓
Program executes in background WP
         ↓
Results stored in spool (SP01)
         ↓
Job status → Finished / Cancelled
```

