## 13.1 Transport Request — Full Structure

```
TRANSPORT REQUEST HIERARCHY:
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Transport Request (Header): DEVK900123
│   Owner : JSMITH
│   Type  : Workbench (K) or Customizing (W)
│   Status: Modifiable → Released
│
├── Task 1 (Subtask): DEVK900124
│   Owner: JSMITH
│   Contains: Objects changed by JSMITH
│   ├── Object 1: ABAP Program ZREPORT01
│   └── Object 2: Function Module Z_GET_DATA
│
└── Task 2 (Subtask): DEVK900125
    Owner: MWEBER
    Contains: Objects changed by MWEBER
    └── Object 3: Table Entry (customizing)

RELEASE SEQUENCE (CRITICAL!):
  ► ALWAYS release TASKS (subtasks) FIRST
  ► THEN release the main REQUEST
  ► You CANNOT release a request with unreleased tasks!
```

## 13.2 Transport Request Naming Convention

```
Format: <SID>K<6-digit-number>

Examples:
  DEVK900123  → DEV system, Workbench request
  DEVK900124  → DEV system, another Workbench request
  QASK100045  → QAS system request

File Names on OS (/usr/sap/trans/):
  data/R900123.DEV   → Data file (contains object data)
  cofiles/K900123.DEV → Control file (contains metadata)

Both files are REQUIRED for import!
If either is missing → transport will fail!
```

