## 13.4 Releasing a Transport Request

```
Transaction: SE09 or SE10

STEP 1: Find your transport request
  SE09 → Select:
    User       : your username
    Status     : ✅ Modifiable  (unreleased)
    Request Type: ✅ Workbench

STEP 2: Expand the request to see tasks

STEP 3: Release TASKS first (subtasks)
  Select Task → Click Release button (truck icon) 🚚
  Confirm → Task status changes to: Released

STEP 4: Release the main REQUEST
  Select Request → Click Release button 🚚
  What happens during release:
    ► SAP locks all objects in the request
    ► R3trans exports objects to /usr/sap/trans/data/
    ► Control file created in /usr/sap/trans/cofiles/
    ► Request status: Modifiable → Released
    ► Transport appears in target system import queue (QAS)

STEP 5: Verify
  Check that files exist on OS:
    ls -la /usr/sap/trans/data/R<number>.<SID>
    ls -la /usr/sap/trans/cofiles/K<number>.<SID>
```

