## 13.6 Transport Request — Best Practices

```
✅ DO:
  ► One transport = one logical change (e.g., one bug fix)
  ► Add meaningful descriptions to every request
  ► Test in DEV before releasing
  ► Keep related objects in the same transport
  ► Document transport in change management tool (SolMan/JIRA)
  ► Verify files exist on OS after release

❌ DON'T:
  ► Put unrelated changes in one transport
  ► Release without testing in DEV
  ► Import to PRD without QAS testing
  ► Leave old modifiable requests open for months
  ► Import to PRD on Friday afternoon!

⚠️ EMERGENCY TRANSPORT PROCEDURE:
  Emergency = Hotfix needed directly in PRD
  
  Step 1: Get written approval from management
  Step 2: Create "Transport of Copies" (not normal transport)
  Step 3: Import to PRD only (skip normal QAS route)
  Step 4: Immediately create parallel normal transport
  Step 5: Import normal transport to QAS for proper testing
  Step 6: Document everything in change management system
