## 14.2 Performing an Import — Complete Guide

```
SCENARIO: Import transport DEVK900123 from DEV to QAS

PRE-IMPORT CHECKLIST:
  □ Change management approval obtained?
  □ Is QAS system running (SM51)?
  □ Enough disk space in /usr/sap/trans/?
  □ No users actively testing in QAS?  
  □ Other pending transports analyzed for conflicts?

STEP 1: Collect Queue
  STMS → QAS Queue → Refresh (F5)
  ► SAP reads /usr/sap/trans/buffer/QAS
  ► New transports appear in the queue

STEP 2: Select Transport(s)
  Option A: Select ONE specific transport
  Option B: Select ALL transports (sequential import)

STEP 3: Set Import Options
  Click "Import" icon or F6:
  
  ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
  │ Target Client  : 200                                    │
  │                                                          │
  │ Options:                                                 │
  │ ✅ Import in Background (ALWAYS recommended!)           │
  │ ✅ Leave Transport Request in Queue                     │
  │    (Keeps in queue after import for re-import if needed)│
  │ ✅ Ignore Invalid Component Version                     │
  │    (Avoid errors for minor version mismatches)         │
  │ □  Overtake Transport Request                          │
  │    (Re-import already imported transport)               │
  │ □  No Transport Log Check                              │
  │    (Skip log validation — use with caution)             │
  └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

STEP 4: Execute Import
  Press OK → Import starts as background job

STEP 5: Monitor Import
  STMS → Queue → Select transport → Logs (Ctrl+F9)
  
  OR: SM37 → Job name: RDDIMPDP → Monitor execution

STEP 6: Check Return Code
  After completion, check RC column in STMS:
  
  RC = 0  → ✅ Perfect — no issues
  RC = 4  → ⚠️ Warning — imported but review logs
  RC = 8  → ❌ Error — import had problems, check logs!
  RC = 12 → ❌ Serious error — objects may be incomplete
  RC = 16 → 🆘 Critical error — system may be affected!
  
⚠️ NEVER ignore RC=8 or higher in production!
   Always investigate before proceeding.
```

