## 14.4 tp Command — OS Level Transport Tool

```
tp is the Transport Program that physically executes imports.
STMS is just a GUI wrapper around tp.

Key tp Commands:
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Display tp version
tp -V

# Show import buffer for system QAS
tp showbuffer QAS pf=/usr/sap/trans/bin/TP_DOMAIN_QAS.PFL

# Import specific transport to QAS client 200
tp import DEVK900123 QAS \
   pf=/usr/sap/trans/bin/TP_DOMAIN_QAS.PFL \
   client=200 \
   U128         ← Options flag (128 = leave in queue)

# Import ALL transports in buffer to QAS
tp import all QAS \
   pf=/usr/sap/trans/bin/TP_DOMAIN_QAS.PFL \
   client=200

# Check return code
echo $?

# Export a transport manually (rarely needed)
tp export DEVK900123 \
   pf=/usr/sap/trans/bin/TP_DOMAIN_DEV.PFL

# Verify transport files integrity
tp checkimpdp QAS \
   pf=/usr/sap/trans/bin/TP_DOMAIN_QAS.PFL

tp Option Flags (U value):
  U000 → Normal import (remove from queue after import)
  U128 → Leave in queue after import (recommended!)
  U256 → Ignore invalid component version
  U512 → Overtake (re-import)
  Combined: U384 = U128 + U256 (leave in queue + ignore version)
```

