## 16.4 Applying Support Packages (SPAM) — Step-by-Step

```
Transaction: SPAM → Support Package Manager

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
PRE-STEPS:
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
1. Download from SAP Support Portal:
   https://support.sap.com → Software Downloads
   → Support Packages and Patches
   → Browse by: Application → SAP ERP (or S/4HANA)
   → Download the complete stack (.SAR files)

2. Upload to SAP system:
   CG3Z → Upload files to /usr/sap/trans/EPS/in/
   OR: Copy .SAR files directly to OS path:
       /usr/sap/trans/EPS/in/

3. Pre-checks:
   □ Full system backup completed?
   □ No open repairs? (SE03 → Object lock check)
   □ No running background jobs? (SM37)
   □ All users logged off? (AL08)
   □ Enough disk space? (df -h)
   □ SPAM itself is at latest version? (SPAM → Spam/Saint version)

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
SPAM IMPORT STEPS:
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
Step 1: SPAM → Load Packages
  ► SPAM reads /usr/sap/trans/EPS/in/
  ► Extracts and registers the packages
  ► Available packages appear in SPAM

Step 2: Display/Define Queue
  SPAM → Support Package → Load Packages → Define Queue
  ► Select the target support package level
  ► SPAM automatically orders dependencies
  ► Queue shows all SPs to be imported in sequence

Step 3: Check Queue
  SPAM → Check Queue
  ► Validates that SPs can be applied (prerequisites)
  ► Checks for open repairs and modifications
  ► Must be GREEN before proceeding!

Step 4: Import Queue
  SPAM → Import → Start Queue import
  ► Runs in background (takes 1-8 hours depending on size)
  ► DO NOT interrupt! Stopping mid-import = complex recovery!
  ► Monitor: SPAM refresh periodically

Step 5: Verify Completion
  SPAM → Status → All SPs show: Successfully imported ✅
  
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
POST-STEPS:
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
1. SU25 → Update authorization profile data
   (New auth objects delivered with SPs must be activated)

2. SGEN → Generate ABAP load (optional but recommended)
   Regenerates all ABAP programs for better performance

3. Test key business transactions

4. Check SM21 for any post-import errors

5. Repeat the process for QAS, then PRD
```

