## 23.2 Memory Types — Detailed Explanation

### 1. Extended Memory (EM)
```
WHAT IT IS:
  ► Main shared memory pool used by ALL work processes
  ► Each user context (dialog step) gets a slice of EM
  ► Most important memory area in SAP
  ► Lives in shared memory segment on OS

HOW IT WORKS:
  User logs in → SAP creates a user context
  User context stored in EM
  WP takes user context from EM → processes request
  WP returns context to EM → WP is free for next request

  This is WHY one WP can serve many users!
  (Unlike dedicated connection model)

PARAMETER:
  em/initial_size_MB = 3000    ← Set to ~50-60% of available RAM
  em/blocksize_kB    = 1024    ← Allocation block size

WHEN IT'S TOO SMALL:
  ► Users get memory errors
  ► ABAP dump: TSV_TNEW_PAGE_ALLOC_FAILED
  ► System falls back to HEAP (PRIV mode)
  ► Performance degrades significantly

MONITORING:
  SM66 → Many WPs in PRIV → EM is too small
  ST02 → Check EM usage percentage
```

### 2. Roll Memory (Roll Buffer)
```
WHAT IT IS:
  ► Stores user context BETWEEN dialog steps
  ► Think of it as a "parking lot" for user sessions
  ► While WP processes another user, your context parks here

HOW IT WORKS:
  User presses ENTER → WP picks up request
  WP needs context → Roll IN from Roll Buffer to EM
  WP finishes → Roll OUT context back to Roll Buffer
  WP is now FREE for another user

PARAMETERS:
  ztta/roll_area      = 3000000   ← Roll area per user (bytes)
  ztta/roll_extension = 3000000   ← Extended roll area per user

WHEN IT'S TOO SMALL:
  ► Users get "Roll area full" in SM21
  ► Error: "Not enough roll memory"
```

### 3. Heap Memory (Private Memory)
```
WHAT IT IS:
  ► Private memory allocated to a SPECIFIC work process
  ► Only used when Extended Memory is exhausted
  ► WP in HEAP = WP in PRIV mode

CONSEQUENCES OF HEAP USE:
  ► WP becomes EXCLUSIVELY tied to one user (PRIV)
  ► WP cannot serve other users while in PRIV
  ► Reduces available WPs for other users
  ► Causes slow response for everyone else!

PARAMETERS:
  abap/heap_area_dia   = 200000000   ← Heap per dialog WP (bytes)
  abap/heap_area_nondia= 300000000   ← Heap per background WP
  abap/heap_area_total = 2000000000  ← Max total heap all WPs

WHEN A WP ENTERS PRIV:
  1. User runs memory-intensive program
  2. EM is full → WP allocates from Heap
  3. WP is now in PRIV (visible in SM66)
  4. After user finishes → WP is RESTARTED (!) 
     SAP AUTOMATICALLY restarts PRIV WPs after use
     This is normal behavior — don't panic!
```

### 4. Paging Area
```
WHAT IT IS:
  ► Overflow area when Extended Memory is full
  ► Stored partially in shared memory, partially on disk
  ► Much slower than EM (disk access!)

PARAMETERS:
  rdisp/PG_SHM   = 50    ← Paging in shared memory (MB)
  rdisp/PG_MAXFS = 32000 ← Paging on filesystem (KB)

MONITORING:
  SM21 → "Paging area full" messages = serious memory issue!
  ST02 → Paging area usage

⚠️ Heavy paging = system is seriously memory-constrained!
   Fix: Increase em/initial_size_MB first!
```

