## 23.4 Memory Sizing Formula

```
RULE OF THUMB FOR SAP MEMORY SIZING:

Total Server RAM Required:
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════

  Extended Memory (EM)     = 50-60% of Total Server RAM
  OS Reserved              = 2-4 GB (OS needs some!)
  Database SGA/Buffer      = 30-40% (if DB on same server)
  SAP Buffers              = 1-2 GB
  Heap + Roll + Paging     = Remainder

EXAMPLE: Server with 64 GB RAM (SAP + Oracle on same server)
───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  OS                  :  4 GB
  Oracle SGA          : 20 GB  (30%)
  SAP Extended Memory : 30 GB  (em/initial_size_MB = 30000)
  SAP Buffers         :  4 GB
  Heap + Roll + Page  :  6 GB
  Total               : 64 GB ✅

EXAMPLE: Dedicated SAP App Server (No DB), 64 GB RAM
───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  OS                  :  4 GB
  SAP Extended Memory : 40 GB  (em/initial_size_MB = 40000)
  SAP Buffers         :  8 GB
  Heap + Roll + Page  : 12 GB
  Total               : 64 GB ✅

⚠️ These are starting guidelines!
   Monitor ST02 and SM66 after go-live
   and tune based on actual usage patterns.
```

