## 24.6 SAP HANA Administration Essentials (2022 Update)

```
For Basis admins managing S/4HANA or BW/4HANA systems:

HANA KEY ADMINISTRATION TASKS:
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

1. HANA COCKPIT (Replaced HANA Studio for most tasks):
   URL: https://<hana-server>:51014
   Login: SYSTEM user or admin user
   
   Capabilities:
   ► System overview and health
   ► Memory / CPU monitoring
   ► Database backup and recovery
   ► Alert monitoring
   ► User administration

2. HANA BACKUP (Critical!):
   HANA backup types:
   ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
   │ Type          │ Description              │ Frequency     │
   ├───────────────┼──────────────────────────┼───────────────┤
   │ Data Backup   │ Full snapshot of all data│ Daily/Weekly  │
   │ Log Backup    │ Transaction log backup   │ Every 15 min  │
   │ Data Snapshot │ Storage snapshot hook    │ As needed     │
   └───────────────┴──────────────────────────┴───────────────┘
   
   Enable Automatic Log Backup:
   HANA Cockpit → Backup Settings → Log Mode = Normal
   Log Backup Path: /hana/backup/log/
   
   Schedule Data Backup via SQL:
   BACKUP DATA USING FILE ('/hana/backup/data/FULL_$(SID)_$(TIMESTAMP)')

3. HANA MEMORY MANAGEMENT:
   Key HANA Memory Concepts:
   ► Column Store    → Main data store (in RAM)
   ► Row Store       → Configuration, catalog data
   ► Code + Stack    → HANA engine itself
   
   Monitor Memory:
   SELECT * FROM M_MEMORY_OVERVIEW;
   
   Key metrics:
   USED_PHYSICAL_MEMORY  → Actual RAM used by HANA
   FREE_PHYSICAL_MEMORY  → Available RAM
   ALLOCATION_LIMIT      → Max HANA can use
   
   HANA Memory Parameters:
   global.ini → [memorymanager]
   global_allocation_limit = 0    ← 0 = auto (90% of RAM)
   
4. HANA USER MANAGEMENT:
   HANA has its own user store (separate from SAP ABAP!)
   
   Key users:
   SYSTEM    → Master admin (like SAP*)
   <SID>ADM  → OS level admin (not in HANA directly)
   SAPABAP1  → SAP ABAP schema owner (DB connection user)
   
   Create HANA user via SQL:
   CREATE USER MONUSER PASSWORD "Monitor1234!" 
     NO FORCE_FIRST_PASSWORD_CHANGE;
   GRANT MONITORING TO MONUSER;
   
   Transaction in ABAP (for SAP-level DB user):
   DB19 → Database user overview
   DB20 → Update database statistics

5. HANA ALERT MONITORING:
   Alerts visible in: HANA Cockpit → Alert section
   Or via SQL:
   SELECT * FROM M_ALERTS 
   WHERE ALERT_RATING >= 3    ← 3=Warning, 4=Error, 5=Critical
   ORDER BY ALERT_TIMESTAMP DESC;
   
   Common HANA Alerts:
   ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
   │ Alert                    │ Action                        │
   ├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────┤
   │ Memory usage > 90%       │ Add RAM or reduce allocation  │
   │ Disk space < 10%         │ Increase disk or clean up     │
   │ Log backup failed        │ Check backup path/permissions │
   │ Delta merge needed       │ Schedule manual delta merge   │
   │ Statistics server stopped│ Restart statistics service   │
   └──────────────────────────┴───────────────────────────────┘
