## Essential SAP OS Commands Reference

```bash
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
SAP PROCESS MANAGEMENT:
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Switch to SAP admin user
su - <sid>adm                # e.g., su - devadm

# Start SAP system
startsap all                  # Start all instances
startsap r3                   # Start ABAP only

# Stop SAP system
stopsap all                   # Stop all (graceful)
stopsap r3                    # Stop ABAP only

# Check process status
sapcontrol -nr 00 -function GetProcessList
sapcontrol -nr 00 -function StartSystem ALL
sapcontrol -nr 00 -function StopSystem ALL

# Check all SAP processes
ps -ef | grep <SID>

═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
KERNEL AND VERSION:
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Check kernel version
/usr/sap/<SID>/SYS/exe/run/disp+work -V

# Check tp version (transport program)
/usr/sap/trans/bin/tp -V

# List kernel executables
ls -la /usr/sap/<SID>/SYS/exe/run/

═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
TRANSPORT COMMANDS:
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Show import buffer
tp showbuffer QAS pf=<profile>

# Import specific transport
tp import DEVK900123 QAS pf=<profile> client=200 U128

# Import all buffered transports
tp import all QAS pf=<profile> client=200 U128

# Check transport files
ls -la /usr/sap/trans/data/
ls -la /usr/sap/trans/cofiles/

═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
FILE AND DISK MANAGEMENT:
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Check disk space (MOST IMPORTANT for Basis!)
df -h

# Check directory size
du -sh /usr/sap/trans/*
du -sh /usr/sap/<SID>/*

# Find large files
find /usr/sap -size +100M -type f 2>/dev/null

# Check SAP work directory traces
ls -ltr /usr/sap/<SID>/DVEBMGS00/work/
cat /usr/sap/<SID>/DVEBMGS00/work/dev_disp

═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
MEMORY AND PERFORMANCE:
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Check OS memory
free -h

# Check swap usage
swapon --show
vmstat 2 5                    # Memory/CPU/IO every 2 sec, 5 times

# Check CPU usage
top
htop                          # Better version of top

# Check I/O performance
iostat -x 2 5

# Check open files (SAP uses MANY!)
lsof -u <sid>adm | wc -l

═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
SAPCAR — ARCHIVE TOOL:
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Extract SAR file
./SAPCAR -xvf filename.SAR

# Extract to specific directory
./SAPCAR -xvf filename.SAR -R /tmp/extract/

# List contents without extracting
./SAPCAR -tvf filename.SAR
```

